stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PowerUp

    state "Power Up" as PowerUp
    state "GPS Lock" as GPSLock
    state "Awaiting Start" as AwaitingStart
    state "Game Initialisation" as GameInit
    state "Game Running" as GameRunning
    state "Dead" as Dead
    state "FTP Mode" as FTP
    state "OTA Mode" as OTA
    state "Network Provisioning" as Provisioning
    state "IR Test" as IRTest

    PowerUp --> FTP : After 2s, trigger + reload held
    PowerUp --> OTA : After 2s, trigger + zoom held
    PowerUp --> Provisioning : After 2s, trigger + right held
    PowerUp --> IRTest : After 2s, trigger + left held
    PowerUp --> AwaitingStart : After 2s, left + right held
    PowerUp --> GPSLock : After 2s, no mode shortcut selected

    GPSLock --> AwaitingStart : GPS position acquired

    AwaitingStart --> GameInit : Valid StartGame command, system time accepted, Wi-Fi shutdown delay elapsed

    GameInit --> GameRunning : Game delay elapsed

    GameRunning --> Dead : Player health reaches zero

    Provisioning --> GPSLock : Configuration saved

    note right of PowerUp
        The startup state waits 2 seconds
        before selecting the operating mode.
        Shortcut combinations are checked
        in the order shown in the source.
    end note

    note right of GPSLock
        Navigation is updated continuously.
        A valid position advances to
        Awaiting Start.
    end note

    note right of AwaitingStart
        Wi-Fi/network service is started.
        The game starts only after a valid
        StartGame command has supplied a
        time accepted by SystemTime::Reset.
        A short exit pacer allows the
        network acknowledgement to be sent.
    end note

    note right of GameInit
        Displays the map and countdown.
        The state waits until gameDelayTime
        has elapsed before starting gameplay.
    end note

    note right of GameRunning
        Gameplay continues while the player
        is alive. Incoming valid hits and
        zone damage can reduce health to zero.
    end note

    note right of FTP
        FTP mode runs its FTP server and
        network broadcasts. Run() returns
        the FTP state continuously.
    end note

    note right of OTA
        OTA mode services ArduinoOTA.
        Run() returns the OTA state
        continuously.
    end note

    note right of Provisioning
        Starts a Wi-Fi access point and
        configuration web server.
        Saving configuration returns to
        GPS Lock.
    end note

    note right of IRTest
        IR test mode receives and transmits
        laser-tag packets. Run() returns
        the IR test state continuously.
    end note

    note right of Dead
        Plays the dead sound and displays
        the dead screen. The current
        implementation has no exit
        transition from this state.
    end note
